# AGENTS.md

## Product
Build "Global Game Community Radar", a web app for game community operators to detect rising global topics, negative sentiment, and community opportunities.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Prisma
- PostgreSQL
- OpenAI service layer with mock fallback
- No external API integration in MVP unless explicitly requested

## Coding Rules
- Keep changes minimal and focused.
- Do not rewrite unrelated files.
- Do not add heavy infrastructure unless requested.
- Prefer simple readable code over complex architecture.
- Use mock data when API keys are missing.
- Add or update tests for scoring and clustering logic.
- Update README when setup or commands change.

## MVP Scope
Pages:
- /dashboard
- /topics/[id]
- /games
- /sources
- /reports

Core features:
- Game management
- Source management
- Mock community posts
- Topic clustering by keyword similarity
- Hot score calculation
- Topic detail page
- Daily report export as Markdown

## Out of Scope for MVP
- Full Discord integration
- X/Twitter integration
- TikTok scraping
- Kafka
- ClickHouse
- Complex vector search
- Multi-tenant billing
- Login system
- Realtime websocket dashboard

## Product Logic
Hot score should not be simple post count. Use:
hot_score =
0.30 * volume_velocity
+ 0.20 * engagement_velocity
+ 0.15 * platform_spread
+ 0.10 * region_spread
+ 0.15 * sentiment_risk
+ 0.10 * novelty_score

Topic categories:
- version_update
- character_balance
- event_feedback
- bug_server_issue
- monetization_p2w
- cheating_bot
- streamer_kol_event
- meme_ugc
- competitor_comparison
- launch_feedback
- refund_review_bomb
- community_mood

## Before Finishing
Run:
- npm run lint
- npm run test
- npm run build

If a command fails, explain the reason and fix it when possible.
